WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:02.479
- [Interviewer] You went
to the hospital for what?

00:00:02.479 --> 00:00:03.460
- Heat stroke

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:04.293
- Heat stroke?

00:00:04.293 --> 00:00:05.126
Today?

00:00:05.126 --> 00:00:05.959
- Yeah.

00:00:06.850 --> 00:00:09.117
I tried to make it back
faster, but I couldn't.

00:00:09.117 --> 00:00:10.350
- That's okay.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:11.183
I'm here.

00:00:11.183 --> 00:00:12.016
You're here.

00:00:14.204 --> 00:00:16.677
- I made it back alive.

00:00:16.677 --> 00:00:18.060
Let's put it that way.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.614
- Yes. So, Tammy, where
are you from originally?

00:00:22.614 --> 00:00:23.610
- Here. L.A.

00:00:23.610 --> 00:00:24.443
- You're from L.A.

00:00:24.443 --> 00:00:26.175
And how long, how long have
you been living on the street?

00:00:26.175 --> 00:00:27.230
- 41 years.

00:00:27.230 --> 00:00:29.230
- And what, what were the circumstances

00:00:29.230 --> 00:00:30.872
that got you down here?

00:00:30.872 --> 00:00:34.371
- Bullies, homeless, mental
illness, in succession

00:00:34.371 --> 00:00:36.550
when I gave up meth.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.552
- Mental illness?

00:00:37.552 --> 00:00:38.385
- Yeah.

00:00:38.385 --> 00:00:39.735
- The bullies bullied me so much

00:00:39.735 --> 00:00:42.402
that I ended up with depression.

00:00:45.423 --> 00:00:46.881
- Do you have a family?

00:00:46.881 --> 00:00:47.714
- Nope.

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:51.953
Not as far as I'm concerned.

00:00:51.953 --> 00:00:54.435
- What do you mean, not as
far as you're concerned?

00:00:54.435 --> 00:00:58.765
- In other words, they're
a bunch of assholes.

00:00:58.765 --> 00:00:59.940
- Say that again, please.

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:00.843
- They're a bunch of assholes.

00:01:00.843 --> 00:01:03.319
I had bullies in the family,

00:01:03.319 --> 00:01:04.819
bullies at school.

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:10.700
You know, everything's
negative it brings you down.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:12.270
- What do you do for money here?

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:14.930
- I panhandle my benefits.

00:01:14.930 --> 00:01:17.601
- Do you get the government stuff?

00:01:17.601 --> 00:01:19.590
- Yeah. Why do you think I pay for this?

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:21.010
- Yeah. Nice tent.

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:23.183
- Yeah, I've got to back it up when I can.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:26.713
- I can.

00:01:26.713 --> 00:01:28.013
- And where do you go to eat?

00:01:28.013 --> 00:01:30.126
- I cook right here. I don't-

00:01:30.126 --> 00:01:31.874
I can't eat most of the food they have.

00:01:31.874 --> 00:01:32.707
- You cook here?

00:01:32.707 --> 00:01:34.361
- Yeah, I've got a stove over there.

00:01:34.361 --> 00:01:35.342
(laughs)

00:01:35.342 --> 00:01:37.058
- Good for you.

00:01:37.058 --> 00:01:38.999
- I take care of myself .

00:01:38.999 --> 00:01:40.249
The best I can.

00:01:54.327 --> 00:01:56.170
- Is this how you pass the time?

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:57.740
- Yeah.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:58.573
- Nice.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.080
- Can we grab a soda on the way?

00:02:02.080 --> 00:02:02.913
- Sure.

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:09.007
I'll grab you dinner, too, if you want.

00:02:10.967 --> 00:02:13.220
- I'll have the same thing you have,

00:02:13.220 --> 00:02:14.699
how's that?

00:02:14.699 --> 00:02:15.532
- You'll what?

00:02:15.532 --> 00:02:16.720
- I'll eat the same thing you do.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:17.553
- There you go.

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:21.930
I think that means we're dating, Tammy.

00:02:25.300 --> 00:02:27.137
Do you have friends here on the street?

00:02:27.137 --> 00:02:30.627
- Nah, I don't consider
nobody out here my friend.

00:02:30.627 --> 00:02:33.731
That would be totally whacked.

00:02:33.731 --> 00:02:35.126
- So, you have contact
with anybody outside?

00:02:35.126 --> 00:02:36.380
- No one.

00:02:36.380 --> 00:02:37.759
- So, it's just you all by yourself?

00:02:37.759 --> 00:02:38.592
- Yeah.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:43.297
- Do you get lonely?
Depressed? Anything like that?

00:02:43.297 --> 00:02:44.661
- Not from that.

00:02:44.661 --> 00:02:47.721
It's when they lie to me
and try to steal my shit.

00:02:47.721 --> 00:02:49.526
That's what gets me.

00:02:49.526 --> 00:02:50.359
Here.

00:02:52.392 --> 00:02:53.942
- Beautiful. I'd love to start.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:57.720
- Sorry. I missed you.

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:58.553
- It's okay.

00:02:58.553 --> 00:02:59.980
- But I'm okay.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:01.718
I got my head-

00:03:01.718 --> 00:03:02.970
You know what I did?

00:03:02.970 --> 00:03:04.520
After they jumped me I laid back down

00:03:04.520 --> 00:03:06.220
and said fuck that and
stuck my head in the sink

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:09.403
and shook my head off
and bucked out the door.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:13.970
I just had to be by myself, my way.

00:03:13.970 --> 00:03:16.470
Cool off as I go.

00:03:16.470 --> 00:03:17.303
- You're a survivor.

00:03:17.303 --> 00:03:19.710
- Yeah, that what I learned
to do with heat stroke,

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:20.683
cool off quick-

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.893
but I took it slow coming back.

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:27.580
Took all the shady sides of the street,

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:29.393
which is what I forgot, you know?

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:33.540
- What's what's the worst thing
that's happened to you here?

00:03:34.959 --> 00:03:37.000
- I'll just put it this way.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:39.240
Some guy tried to attack me in my tent

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:40.733
when I told him no, go away.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.680
Shit like that happens all the time.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:44.513
- Yeah.

00:03:44.513 --> 00:03:46.418
- Hey, these guys out here think

00:03:46.418 --> 00:03:49.279
they're the boss of everything.

00:03:49.279 --> 00:03:50.370
- You've been raped here?

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:55.050
- No, the one that tried got stabbed.

00:03:55.050 --> 00:03:56.040
- What's that?

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:58.280
- The one that tried got stabbed.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:03:59.188
- Oh, is that right?

00:03:59.188 --> 00:04:00.296
- With a pen.

00:04:00.296 --> 00:04:02.312
- Good for you.

00:04:02.312 --> 00:04:03.395
Good for you.

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:08.273
- He's lucky I didn't get
me knitting needle out.

00:04:08.273 --> 00:04:09.690
(laughs)

00:04:09.690 --> 00:04:11.980
Or the crochet I had would've been worse,

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:12.813
the Afghan hook.

00:04:12.813 --> 00:04:15.350
It's like I have crochet hook.

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:19.380
I have a knitting needle about that long.

00:04:19.380 --> 00:04:20.320
- That'll hurt.

00:04:20.320 --> 00:04:22.850
- Yeah, but there's
more going out than in.

00:04:22.850 --> 00:04:25.583
- Oh, that's right. It's
got a hook at the end.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:30.205
- There was a point in
time when I've thought

00:04:30.205 --> 00:04:33.392
society was so dysfunctional,

00:04:33.392 --> 00:04:34.743
it might've made me normal.

00:04:36.130 --> 00:04:37.480
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:38.930
You're not too far off there.

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:40.813
- Sorry about that.

00:04:42.011 --> 00:04:42.844
- About what?

00:04:44.776 --> 00:04:49.120
- They say a high IQ comes
with a mental illness

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:50.440
that was along for the ride.

00:04:50.440 --> 00:04:53.802
- Yeah, I buy some of that.

00:04:53.802 --> 00:04:56.580
- I heard it on a radio talk show.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:04:58.040
I was flipping through

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:00.247
trying to find some rock
and roll and I heard it.

00:05:00.247 --> 00:05:01.443
- Tell me about your childhood.

00:05:03.062 --> 00:05:05.690
- It was only the worst
nightmare and that was it.

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:06.523
- Why's that?

00:05:07.597 --> 00:05:09.460
- Adoption.

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:10.293
- Oh, you were adopted?

00:05:10.293 --> 00:05:11.126
- Yeah.

00:05:11.126 --> 00:05:11.959
- At what age? Like right away?

00:05:11.959 --> 00:05:12.908
- Three and a half.

00:05:12.908 --> 00:05:13.741
- Three and a half?

00:05:13.741 --> 00:05:14.574
What happened to your parents?

00:05:14.574 --> 00:05:16.470
- I don't know.

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:19.770
I found out my brother died
on the way to the hospital

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:23.053
from something or another
that happened at the home,

00:05:24.379 --> 00:05:27.910
and I decided not to find out anymore.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:29.783
I dreaded it was abuse.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:33.053
- Did you ever have contact

00:05:33.053 --> 00:05:33.886
with your real parents after that?

00:05:33.886 --> 00:05:34.719
- No.

00:05:34.719 --> 00:05:35.552
- Never.

00:05:35.552 --> 00:05:36.670
- Never even bothered.

00:05:36.670 --> 00:05:40.723
I got about three paragraphs
in my bedroom and tossed it.

00:05:43.590 --> 00:05:44.423
Yeah.

00:05:44.423 --> 00:05:45.383
- Oh, you didn't even read it?

00:05:47.890 --> 00:05:49.407
- The brother I would have had died

00:05:49.407 --> 00:05:51.980
and my other sister had Down Syndrome.

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:52.813
- Really?

00:05:52.813 --> 00:05:53.646
- Yep.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:56.940
- You're lucky one.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.422
- Nah, not really.

00:05:58.422 --> 00:05:59.789
They're better off.

00:05:59.789 --> 00:06:02.550
(laughs)

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:04.400
She gets taken care of

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:06.743
and he don't have to suffer about nothing.

00:06:09.750 --> 00:06:10.970
- And you have children?
How many children?

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:11.803
- No kids

00:06:11.803 --> 00:06:12.636
- No kids?

00:06:12.636 --> 00:06:13.469
- Nope.

00:06:13.469 --> 00:06:14.699
- I thought you said they're all assholes.

00:06:14.699 --> 00:06:16.098
- That was your family.

00:06:16.098 --> 00:06:17.290
- Yeah.

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:18.870
- Never married?

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:21.310
- Four times, they was real assholes.

00:06:21.310 --> 00:06:22.540
- Oh, you were married how many times?

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:23.373
- Four.

00:06:23.373 --> 00:06:24.206
- Four times?

00:06:24.206 --> 00:06:26.454
- Yeah, jerk magnet is what I figured.

00:06:26.454 --> 00:06:27.287
- What's that?

00:06:27.287 --> 00:06:28.120
- Jerk magnet.

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:30.230
- You're a jerk magnet?

00:06:30.230 --> 00:06:31.090
- Yeah.

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:32.620
- You're funny.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:36.108
- There's the easier,
softer way of putting it.

00:06:36.108 --> 00:06:37.580
- Okay.

00:06:37.580 --> 00:06:39.510
- What's the harsher way of putting it?

00:06:39.510 --> 00:06:41.070
- It was son of a bitches.

00:06:43.001 --> 00:06:43.834
- Yeah, I like jerk magnet.

00:06:43.834 --> 00:06:44.710
That's a good one.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:49.290
- Hey, at least I found
a way to laugh at it.

00:06:50.840 --> 00:06:53.190
- Do you have plans for down the road?

00:06:53.190 --> 00:06:54.730
- Not really.

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:58.393
- Just muddle through until
it's my time to go see God.

00:07:00.270 --> 00:07:02.220
Because that's all we really do anyway.

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:04.243
- Yeah.

